    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Durable enqueue rejections (/v1/rejections)",
      "description": "Record-level drill-down of admission-time enqueue rejections from the read-only /v1/rejections feed. These enqueues never created a job row, so this is the only durable per-event trail. For a circuit_breaker or chain_quarantine row, trace_id is the lineage handle (search it in /v1/search) and parent_id is the depth-N job the offending handler tried to descend from. Records are retained independently of job history (ANVILMQ_RETENTION_REJECTIONS_AGE_MS, default 7d), so they survive even after the referenced jobs are pruned. Honors the dashboard time range via since_ms=${__from}.",
      "type": "table",
      "datasource": {
